The lamp room at the top of the lighthouse, at dusk. Brass, glass, the great lens. ROSALIND trims the wick. MORDECAI sits on an upturned bucket with a notebook he has not written in.

MORDECAI
The report wants a number. Cost per ship guided, per year.

ROSALIND
And what does the number want?

MORDECAI
To be smaller.

ROSALIND
Then divide by more ships. There are more on nights like this.

She lights the lamp. The lens turns. Light sweeps the audience.

MORDECAI
(quietly)
I have read four hundred reports on lights like this. I have never stood in one.

ROSALIND
And?

MORDECAI
It’s louder than I thought. The light. I didn’t think light would be loud.

ROSALIND
That’s the clockwork. And the wind. And you, breathing like you climbed a hundred and twelve steps.

MORDECAI
A hundred and eleven. The ninth one doesn’t count.

ROSALIND laughs for the first time.

ROSALIND
Write that in your report.
